{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2991","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2991","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2991\",\"parent_revision\":\"3edc11d162bee71bfa01692b7b8cf585f67c2bce22268ee5500b3e10b786b8c6\",\"root_revision\":\"3edc11d162bee71bfa01692b7b8cf585f67c2bce22268ee5500b3e10b786b8c6\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-19\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`.github/workflows/code-quality.yml:273` comments the `test-e2e` job as \\\"Advisory: NOT wired into quality-gate until stable run history established.\\\" But the job itself carries no `continue-on-error: true` on its main step (`Run e2e tests`, line ~292) \u2014 only its unrelated cleanup step has it (line 298). So a failure in `test-e2e` still turns the entire `Code quality` workflow run red on `main`, even though the job is supposedly advisory and not meant to block anything.\\n\\n```\\ngh run list -R Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills --workflow \\\"Code quality\\\" --branch main --limit 30\\n\u2192 failure on every run examined, continuous since at least 2026-08-17T04:45Z\\n```\\n\\nEvery one of those failures is `test-e2e`. Inside that \\\"expected\\\" red is a real, separate regression (see the companion item on `operations.py`'s optional response keys) \u2014 but because `main`'s CI has displayed as red for days as a matter of course, a genuine contract break was indistinguishable from the job's normal advisory noise. This is a signal-integrity problem independent of whatever bug `test-e2e` happens to be catching at any given time: an advisory job that can paint the whole run red isn't functioning as advisory.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **ci: test-e2e job has no continue-on-error despite being documented as advisory, reddening every main run** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Workflow-quality review, 2026-08-18/19, re-verified live 2026-08-19\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-19\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"1cf57ba1ef3f8195802013cc5e5dfb7aa37c3c5a3b9e61cf488610fe97d0445b\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPgvuHw\"}"}